ladspa-speakereq (1.2-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Removed the date-based license check; the plugin no longer stops
    equalizing after a fixed expiry date. The "Licensed" output port is
    retained for API compatibility and now always reports 1.
  * Corrected packaging metadata: MIT license (matching LICENSE), HiFiBerry
    as maintainer, and the real upstream repository URLs
  * Documented the vendored inih (utils/ini.c) as BSD-3-Clause
  * Removed stale LV2 references left over from the LADSPA-only refactoring
  * Corrected the documented port layout to the actual 418 ports
  * Fixed invalid LADSPA port hints on the "Enable" and "save_settings"
    ports, which combined LADSPA_HINT_TOGGLED with hints the specification
    does not permit alongside it. The advertised default of "Enable" now
    reads as 1 (process) instead of 0, and so agrees with the value hosts
    were already using. This corrects the advertised metadata only; the
    PipeWire filter chain resolved "Enable" to 1 with the previous hints
    as well, so processing behaviour is unchanged.

 -- HiFiBerry <info@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 13 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200

